[-`Number`'s abstract-]{+each type's own+}
[-declares,-]{+declares in its api (F-324),+}
[-Bindings: `LibraryBuiltin/FortressBuiltin.fss:241`, `:374`, `:383`, `:396`, `:570`; the abstract: `Library/FortressLibrary.fsi:291`; the-]{+The+}
[-**All-]{+**The+}
{+`Generator2Demo` draws its arrays by `random`, so a product of them can overflow in `PROD`, and one such `IntegerOverflow` stop in a run is not a regression.+}
{+on the code that `4445d848b` committed+}
[-3.-]{+3; `compile-ladder/climb-batch-27/REPAIR-review.md`, section 2.+}
{+through the prelude's `Object`,+}
{+though not through the one library's `Object`, whose `asString` is `self.ilkName`;+}
[-`Number`'s `=` compares a float with an exact number after `asFloat`, so-]{+`Number` declares no `=`; each type declares one at each type+}
[-is not transitive (row 434).-]{+coerces from or into (F-324).+}
[-removed-]{+removed,+}
{+before F-324 removed it from the library,+}
[-bound because its-]{+bound, though it has no+}
[-lists every type below it, so an element type excludes `String`; the ring alone does not give that. That exclusion makes the-]{+now (F-324). The+}
[-a valid overloading-]{+stand+}
[-`String`. `Number` also declares the `asFloat` that-]{+`String`, and+}
{+checker finds no error in them (F-53); no run measures what now keeps a scalar `T` apart from `String`. The+}
[-calls.-]{+is declared at each of the eight number types, by its own `asFloat` (F-324).+}

